hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"296","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, told us, Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that a Bedouin urinated in the mosque, and some of them jumped to him. The people, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not force him.” Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it on him."
"297","Utba bin Abdullah Al-Hammadi told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubaid Allah bin told me Abdullah bin Utba said that Abu Hurairah told him that a Bedouin urinated in the mosque, so the people rose up to him to prevent him, so he told them The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave him. Spill some water in his urine, or a log of water. You were only sent as facilitators, and you did not You will be sent to make things difficult.”"
"298","Narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala’, narrated by Sufyan, who said: I memorized it from al-Zuhri. He said: Sa’id told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. H Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub bin Al-Jazari told us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sadaqah, told us: Sufyan, who is Ibn Husayn, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. H Al-Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, so they mentioned the hadith, and in the hadith of Sufyan bin Husayn, He said: “Indeed, there is ease in your religion.”"
